# Netlify reads this file from the publish directory, so it applies under both
# of the wirings netlify.toml describes (base = repo root, or base = site/).
# Redirect rules in a netlify.toml would take precedence over it; neither of
# ours defines any.
#
# The site answers on two hostnames: the custom domain and the Netlify
# subdomain it was first deployed to. Both served 200, so the whole site
# existed twice for a crawler. Every page carries a canonical pointing at the
# custom domain, which is enough for Google to consolidate, but the duplicate
# still gets crawled and can still be linked. This makes the subdomain a
# permanent redirect instead.
#
# The rule matches that exact host, so Netlify's deploy previews and branch
# deploys — deploy-preview-N--<site>.netlify.app — are untouched and stay
# browsable. `301!` forces the redirect: without the bang, a request for a
# path that exists as a static file (which is all of them) would be served
# rather than redirected.

https://vaavkitchenandcaterers.netlify.app/*  https://vaavkitchenandcaterers.com/:splat  301!

# Every page is also reachable at its explicit index.html — /services/ and
# /services/index.html both returned 200, so each page had a second URL. Both
# carry the same canonical, pointing at the clean form, and none of the
# index.html URLs are indexed, so this was never the active problem; it is
# closed here because a duplicate surface that costs nothing to remove should
# not be left open.
#
# Listed one per page rather than pattern-matched: a Netlify splat only binds
# at the end of a path, so no single rule covers both /about/index.html and
# /menu/tiffin/index.html. Nine pages is few enough to be explicit, and the
# list is checked by the redirect test below.
#
# These need the forcing bang for the same reason as the rule above: each
# index.html is a real file in the publish directory and would otherwise be
# served rather than redirected. Requests for the clean URL are unaffected —
# a rule matches the requested path, and "/" is not "/index.html".

/index.html               /               301!
/about/index.html         /about/         301!
/contact/index.html       /contact/       301!
/corporate/index.html     /corporate/     301!
/services/index.html      /services/      301!
/menu/index.html          /menu/          301!
/menu/tiffin/index.html   /menu/tiffin/   301!
/menu/lunch/index.html    /menu/lunch/    301!
/menu/dinner/index.html   /menu/dinner/   301!
